<!--
  robot: irb1100_workcell | consumers: RViz2, robot_state_publisher, Gazebo (gz sim) with gz_ros2_control, CAD viewer
  units: meters, kilograms, radians | frames: +X forward, +Y left, +Z up (REP-103). World frame = floor.
  root: world (frame-only) | file is EXPANDED from urdf/workcell.urdf.xacro, edit the xacro and regenerate.
  source of dimensions:
    IRB 1100-4/0.58: ABB official CAD IRB1100_4kg-580-STD_OmniCore_rev04 (STEP, 2022): visuals, joint axes and origins read from it
    (zero-pose flange face at X=0.364 Z=0.617 from axis 1, wrist centre X=0.300). Limits/speeds from ABB spec 3HAC064993, 21.1 kg total.
    Earlier primitive-shape arm used a wrong 0.064 m offset and is replaced.
    Zimmer LWR50L-23-00006-A: outline (plate dia 75x18, housing 53.8x26, 106 to jaw face), mass 0.725 kg, stroke 10 mm/jaw from the Zimmer datasheet V1;
    envelope shapes only, with cable loop, contact block, jaw guide and jaws (no STEP), jaw orientation about the flange axis assumed, no fingers, LWR50F head not modelled, TCP = jaw mounting face 0.1275 m.
    Table, pallet, blocks, stand: my layout choices (table top 1.1 x 1.1 m square and 25 mm thick (from user), surface z=0.75 (assumed), pallet centre (-0.05,0), robot base (0.20,0.00,0.75)).
  meshes: ../meshes/*.stl (clamp, 2 camera mounts) and ../meshes/irb1100/*.stl (arm: 7 visual meshes ~30k triangles, 7 convex-hull collision meshes), source units mm, scale 0.001, each arm mesh origin = its joint axis frame.
  inertials: arm links = ESTIMATE: 21.1 kg spread over the links by CAD solid volume at uniform density (link_6 set to 0.1 kg), tensors from the voxelised CAD, not measured;
    gripper 0.725 kg (Zimmer datasheet), inertia = uniform box estimate; static scene boxes carry placeholder inertia (fixed to world).
  joints (positive motion, all limits from ABB spec):
    (directions follow the ABB convention, a static CAD cannot confirm them; check on the real robot)
    joint_1 axis +Z: arm turns counter-clockwise seen from above.
    joint_2 axis +Y: upper arm tilts FORWARD (+X). joint_3 axis +Y: forearm tip moves DOWN (-Z) when the forearm points +X.
    joint_4 axis +X: forearm roll, right-hand rule about +X. joint_5 axis +Y: tool tip moves DOWN when the tool points +X.
    joint_6 axis +X: flange rotates right-hand rule about its outward normal.
    Zero pose: upper arm vertical, forearm horizontal, flange pointing +X (ABB home).
  frame-only links: world, tool0 (Z out of flange, ROS-I), gripper_tcp, cam1_optical_frame, cam2_left_optical_frame, cam2_right_optical_frame (z forward, x right, y down).
  cameras: cam1_link / cam2_link x forward, y left, z up. Cam1 pitched 35 deg down, looks along +X. Cam2 looks straight down.
  assumptions:
    gripper jaws are modelled fixed-open (stroke is 10 mm per jaw).
    mount mesh positions (camera centre in mount frame) come from cad/camera_mount.py output for tilt 35 and 90.
    cam2 = ZED Mini (SDK name ZED_M): body 124.5x30.5x26.5 mm, baseline 63 mm, 90 deg HFOV, 1280x720 sim image, per Stereolabs datasheet (lens plane offset 13.25 mm assumed). cam1 still a 90x25x25 mm placeholder, model not chosen.
    plugin parameters path is relative (config/controllers.yaml); the xacro launch passes an absolute path.
-->
